{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00567",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.91,
      "end_seconds": 11.97,
      "duration_seconds": 11.06,
      "text": "Mrs Iyer? Your booking says six-week postnatal check, so let us see how you and the baby are doing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.92,
      "end_seconds": 24.98,
      "duration_seconds": 10.06,
      "text": "Yes, doctor. Baby is sleeping at my mother-in-law's place today. We are both fine, only I am a little tired."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.23,
      "end_seconds": 35.18,
      "duration_seconds": 7.95,
      "text": "A little tired. Tired how? All day long, or at a certain time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.56,
      "end_seconds": 42.86,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "By the evening mostly. In the morning I manage okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.69,
      "end_seconds": 53.85,
      "duration_seconds": 9.16,
      "text": "That is very common with a six-week-old. How many hours are you sleeping in total?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.55,
      "end_seconds": 61.89,
      "duration_seconds": 6.34,
      "text": "Maybe four, but broken. That is normal only, everyone says so."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 64.34,
      "end_seconds": 73.66,
      "duration_seconds": 9.32,
      "text": "Yes, quite normal. And how is your mood? Any low mood, crying spells, anything like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.92,
      "end_seconds": 79.59,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "No, no. I am happy only. Just tired."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.27,
      "end_seconds": 86.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.94,
      "text": "Good to hear. Are you feeding the baby yourself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.1,
      "end_seconds": 93.88,
      "duration_seconds": 6.78,
      "text": "Yes, breastfeeding. Every three hours or so. She is feeding well, thank God."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.32,
      "end_seconds": 107.17,
      "duration_seconds": 10.85,
      "text": "Fine. Does any illness run in your family, say diabetes or thyroid problems? It matters for your check-ups later."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.89,
      "end_seconds": 115.65,
      "duration_seconds": 5.76,
      "text": "Just my mother. She has diabetes, for many years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.96,
      "end_seconds": 126.8,
      "duration_seconds": 8.84,
      "text": "Noted. Now I will check your pressure, pulse, temperature and weight. Please stand on the scale first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.7,
      "end_seconds": 134.22,
      "duration_seconds": 6.52,
      "text": "Okay, doctor. I have been scared to check my weight since the delivery."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.14,
      "end_seconds": 165.54,
      "duration_seconds": 8.4,
      "text": "Weight is 64 kilograms. Blood pressure 112 over 70, pulse 76, temperature 36.6 degrees. All in order."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.37,
      "end_seconds": 170.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "Sixty-four. That is less than I expected, actually."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.23,
      "end_seconds": 180.91,
      "duration_seconds": 7.68,
      "text": "Good. Now lie down, I will press gently on your tummy and check the womb."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.79,
      "end_seconds": 183.62,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "Okay, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.8,
      "end_seconds": 210.35,
      "duration_seconds": 9.55,
      "text": "The womb has gone back to its normal size, and it feels firm. The healing is as expected."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 211.98,
      "end_seconds": 215.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "That is good to hear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.05,
      "end_seconds": 226.42,
      "duration_seconds": 8.37,
      "text": "So overall, this looks like normal postnatal recovery. There is nothing for me to treat today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 227.68,
      "end_seconds": 234.03,
      "duration_seconds": 6.35,
      "text": "Doctor, my husband is asking about family planning. What are the options?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.42,
      "end_seconds": 250.68,
      "duration_seconds": 15.26,
      "text": "Basically four. One, condoms, which you can start right away. Two, an implant in the upper arm. Three, a coil, copper or hormonal. Four, natural cycles, but that is least reliable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 252.1,
      "end_seconds": 255.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "Which one is better while breastfeeding?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.93,
      "end_seconds": 268.28,
      "duration_seconds": 10.35,
      "text": "Condoms, the implant and the copper coil are all fine. Some hormonal methods need more care, so we choose together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 271.11,
      "end_seconds": 278.1,
      "duration_seconds": 6.99,
      "text": "Let me discuss at home first. For now we will manage with condoms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.23,
      "end_seconds": 286.46,
      "duration_seconds": 7.23,
      "text": "Perfectly reasonable. Take your time deciding, there is no hurry on this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 287.29,
      "end_seconds": 294.15,
      "duration_seconds": 6.86,
      "text": "Can I start exercise again? I used to do yoga before pregnancy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.14,
      "end_seconds": 309.67,
      "duration_seconds": 12.53,
      "text": "Start with walking, thirty minutes a day. Add pelvic floor exercises, a few times daily. Slowly build up to yoga over the next month."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 312.36,
      "end_seconds": 318.0,
      "duration_seconds": 5.64,
      "text": "And lifting heavy things? The baby seat is very heavy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.56,
      "end_seconds": 329.05,
      "duration_seconds": 9.49,
      "text": "Lift the baby, yes, but avoid very heavy loads for another few weeks. Let your husband carry the seat."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 330.31,
      "end_seconds": 339.23,
      "duration_seconds": 8.92,
      "text": "He will be happy to hear that. My mother-in-law is also staying with us for two months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 341.25,
      "end_seconds": 351.03,
      "duration_seconds": 9.78,
      "text": "That is a big help, then. Do let her take the night feeds sometimes, if you are expressing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 352.35,
      "end_seconds": 359.06,
      "duration_seconds": 6.71,
      "text": "Yes, both are very supportive. I am joining work after three months only."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 360.38,
      "end_seconds": 371.15,
      "duration_seconds": 10.77,
      "text": "That is a good plan. Eat well, drink plenty of water, and rest when the baby rests."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 372.09,
      "end_seconds": 377.21,
      "duration_seconds": 5.12,
      "text": "I will try, doctor. Thank you for your time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 379.98,
      "end_seconds": 384.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "My pleasure, madam. Go and enjoy that little one."
    }
  ]
}
